Content area from OpenRune/OpenRune-Server#353 (answers there: all of it, one PR per row, ids renumbered against main, wiki data is fine).

From our per-feature patches `12-quests-sheep-shearer-romeo-juliet`, `65-witchs-potion` (in [`openrune/upstream/`](https://github.com/AlexPerrin/osrs-plugins-reverse/tree/main/openrune/upstream) of osrs-plugins-reverse), on `main` (`1be5dfb5f`).

Stacked on the Sheep Shearer / Romeo & Juliet PR (its `QuestTalkFixture`); only the last commit is new here. Merged after that PR, this one shows only its own commit.

**Problem.** Witch's Potion was not implemented.

**Change.** New quest. Progress is varp 67 (`hetty`) through a server-only varbit: 0, 1 started, 2 ingredients given, 3 complete (drunk from the cauldron), the values Quest Helper reads.
- Hetty's dialogue, including the player's line for every combination of held ingredients; the hand-in takes one of each in one transaction.
- Rewards: 1 QP, 325 Magic XP.
- Hetty's after-quest lines move from `RimmingtonTownsfolkScript` into the quest.
- The rat's tail comes from a new rat drop table with the usual quest gate (`quest_mode = "during"`).

Server-only ids, numbered after the ids already on main and not shared with any of our other PRs, so they merge in any order: varbit `witchs_potion_progress` 63718.

**Tests.** `WitchsPotionInteractionTest`, plus the quest suites it builds on.

On this branch (Docker `eclipse-temurin:21`, upstream's `./gradlew`, 4 GB container; a clean `freshCache` of main restored first, then `:or-cache:buildCache :or-cache:mergePluginGamevals`, then each task as a separate run, then `run` to "Server ready"): buildCache pass, `spotlessCheck` pass, `assemble` pass, `test` pass, `integration` pass, boot pass (Server ready in 8.412380001s). `tools/scripts/fix_gameval_conflicts.py --check` finds no conflicts on this branch, nor with all of our open content PRs merged together.

Nothing was checked in game from this exact branch; the in-game checks above were on our own server build (an older main plus these and our other patches).

**Data sources.** OSRS Wiki (by the wiki's contributors, CC BY-NC-SA 3.0, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/3.0/): the dialogue follows the wiki transcript. Step values: Quest Helper (BSD).

**Caveats.**
- With the default quest-requirements mode (assume-completed) the drop-table quest gate never passes, so the rat's tail only drops under respect-progress or virtual-completions. Our own server uses an `NpcDeathKillHook` on the quest stage instead; happy to switch to that if you prefer.
- Guesses: the journal text and the quest scroll item.

**Release note.** Witch's Potion is playable.

